From: NixOS for nabu
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: do not abort system suspend on GPU quiesce
 timeout

The msm GPU driver registers adreno_system_suspend() for every system
sleep transition (SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS maps .suspend, .freeze and
.poweroff to it), and the PM core runs dpm_suspend_start(PMSG_SUSPEND)
for both suspend-to-idle and suspend-to-RAM. When the GPU does not
quiesce within the one-second wait, the callback returns -EBUSY and the
PM core aborts the entire system suspend ("Some devices failed to
suspend"). On sm8150/nabu, where the a6xx GMU suspend sequence is not
fully reliable, this turns every suspend attempt into a failure,
regardless of the mem_sleep mode selected on the command line.

A single wedged device must not veto system sleep. On the timeout path,
fall through to pm_runtime_force_suspend() instead: the a6xx GMU stop
sequence already degrades gracefully (a6xx_gmu_shutdown() self-falls
back to a6xx_gmu_force_off() with bounded waits whenever the GMU is not
responsive), and resume cold-boots the GPU back up from a clean power
state, which is the same recovery the hang path uses.

Approach adapted from the iris VPU5 suspend fix (CFM880/nabu-iris
42085a8, "media: iris: stop aborting suspend on legacy VPU5"): a device
whose power-collapse is incomplete keeps system suspend alive instead
of failing it.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -362,13 +362,20 @@
 				       gpu->active_submits == 0,
 				       msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
 	if (remaining == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * A GPU that failed to quiesce in time must not
+		 * veto system sleep: the s2idle and suspend-to-RAM
+		 * paths both run this callback, so returning an
+		 * error here aborts every suspend attempt. Fall
+		 * through to the shutdown instead: the GMU stop
+		 * sequence degrades to a forced power-off when the
+		 * GMU is not responsive, and resume cold-boots the
+		 * GPU back up.
+		 */
 		dev_err(dev, "Timeout waiting for GPU to suspend\n");
-		ret = -EBUSY;
-		goto out;
 	}
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
-out:
 	if (ret)
 		resume_scheduler(gpu);
 
